# An OEM cipher suite record whose IANA has three distinct, non-zero bytes.
#
# channel_ciph_algmask.tr uses the realistic IANA 0x000157, whose zero most
# significant byte hides the `record->iana[2] << 16` term of ipmi24toh(): drop
# it and the printed IANA is identical.  Here the IANA is 0xf3c2b1, so a
# reversed order (0xb1c2f3), a dropped high byte (0x00c2b1) and a one-byte
# offset slip all print differently.
#
# The record is followed by a standard record so that the OEM record's 8-byte
# size is pinned too: consume the wrong number of bytes and the next record
# starts in the wrong place.
#
# See the "distinct, non-zero bytes" rule in tests/transport/Bmc.zig.
default_ccode 0xc1

respond get_channel_cipher_suites
  netfn 0x06
  cmd 0x54
  data 0e
  # OEM record: start C1h, suite id 81h, IANA b1 c2 f3, algs 01 02 03
  data c1 81 b1 c2 f3 01 02 03
  # standard record: start C0h, suite id 04h, algs 01 41 81
  data c0 04 01 41 81
end
